{
  "enabled": false,
  "name": "Feature flag audit",
  "description": "Manual-trigger audit of every feature flag in the default project (active and archived). Identifies cleanup candidates using metadata returned by the Unleash MCP server. Enable when you want the trigger button to appear in the Hooks panel.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Run a feature flag audit using the Unleash MCP server. Steps: (1) Call list_flags with projectId set to the default project (or whatever the user specifies) and archived=false to enumerate active flags. (2) Call list_flags a second time with archived=true to enumerate archived flags — Unleash exposes active and archived as disjoint result sets, so both calls are required for full inventory. (3) For each flag from both lists, call get_flag_state to retrieve the FeatureDetails (name, type, stale, archived, createdAt, environments[]). (4) Skip flags where type is kill-switch or permission — these are permanent by Unleash's defaults. (5) For each remaining flag, evaluate these signals in order: (a) stale === true → Unleash already flagged it, include in report; (b) archived === true → already archived in Unleash but code references may remain, include for code cleanup; (c) all environments[].lastSeenAt older than 30 days where the flag is enabled → no SDK has hit it, include; (d) age(createdAt) > expected lifetime for type (check steering/cleanup-cadence.md) → overdue, include. (6) Produce a prioritized cleanup report sorted by: stale flags first, then archived flags, then by oldest lastSeenAt across all enabled environments, then by (age - expected lifetime). For each candidate, include: flag name, type, archived status, age in days, oldest lastSeenAt, which signals fired, and suggested next action (e.g., 'run cleanup_flag', 'archive in Unleash first', 'check with feature owner'). (7) Do NOT call cleanup_flag automatically — the report is for the user to triage. (8) If get_flag_state returns no environments[] data for some flags, note that in the report rather than guessing."
  }
}
